You need to have a tool set in the workshop, and a spare part that can be used to fix the bike.

The agent needs to be able to move between the workshop and garage. This can be done by removing the door between the two rooms.

Once the bike is in the workshop, the agent can perform the following actions:
- Pick up the tool set: The agent will pick up the tool set and place it on the work bench.
- Remove the part: The agent will remove the part that is causing the problem.
- Replace the part: The agent will replace the part with the spare part.
- Tighten the screw: The agent will tighten the screw to secure the new part.
- Test ride: The agent will test ride the bike to make sure it is working properly.

